  Step 11: Update & Delete Functioanlitiy for Patient

   We rea already rendering dynamic urls inside patients/list.html
   Eg. /patients/1/edit will be rednered using below code
   <td>
        <a href="/patients/{{ p.id }}/edit" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">Edit</a>
         <a href="/patients/{{ p.id }}/delete" class="btn btn-sm btn-danger ms-2">Delete</a>
    </td>

    Now, when someone clicks on Edit button the GET request is sent to 
    Eg. /patient/1/edit

    Now, we have to receive id from url in backend
    and show patient edit form with his details prefilled

    To acheive that,
     Step 11.1 
      inside patients/urls.py
      urlpatterns = [
          path('', patient_list),
          path('<int:pk>/edit', patient_edit)
      ]

      Here our id from the url which is 1 will be received into variable called 'pk'
     As you can see, the route is mapped to pateint_edit view

      Step 11.2 Update patients/views.py as below
      from django.shortcuts import get_object_or_404
      @login_required
      def patient_edit(request, pk):
          patient = get_object_or_404(Patient, pk=pk)
          return render(request, 'patient_edit.html', {'patient': patient})

      here inside ok paramater we will receive 1 as integer
      Then we are quering database using get_object_or_404
      if pateitn is retreived we are sending to  patient_edit.html

      Step 11.3 Update patient_edit.html to show patient details prefilled
      
      <form method="POST">
          <input type="text" name="name" value="{{ patient.name }}">
          <input type="text" name="phone" value="{{ patient.phone }}">
          <button type="submit">Save</button>
      </form>

      Value attributes are rendered with actual data from patient
      

